.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt AWK 1
.Os NovaOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm awk
.Nd scan records and process fields
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl bS
.Op Fl F Ar fs
.Op Fl v Ar var=value
.Op Fl i Ar library
.Ar program
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Fl f Ar script
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Each pattern selects records on which its action runs. Input defaults to standard input. A missing final newline still terminates a record.
.Pp
BEGIN and END run before and after input. BEGINFILE and ENDFILE run for each file. Use next to skip a record and nextfile to advance to another file. Patterns include regular expressions and inclusive ranges.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl F Ar fs , Fl \-field-separator Ns = Ns Ar fs
Set the input field separator.
.It Fl v Ar var=value , Fl \-assign Ns = Ns Ar var=value
Assign a value before BEGIN. Operand assignments occur between files.
.It Fl f Ar file , Fl \-file Ns = Ns Ar file
Read program source. A dash reads standard input.
.It Fl e Ar text , Fl \-source Ns = Ns Ar text
Append program text in argument order.
.It Fl i Ar file , Fl \-include Ns = Ns Ar file
Include a program file once. AWKPATH supplies search directories.
.It Fl E Ar file , Fl \-exec Ns = Ns Ar file
Read program and stop interpreting options and assignment operands.
.It Fl b , Fl \-characters-as-bytes
Process input as octets.
.It Fl S , Fl \-sandbox
Deny system(), redirected getline, output redirection and shell pipes. Named input operands remain available.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Display localized help.
.It Fl V , Fl \-version
Display localized version information.
.It Fl C , Fl \-copyright
Display the upstream MIT notice.
.El
.Pp
A double dash ends option processing. Unsupported command-line options produce a diagnostic. Dynamic library loading is unavailable.
.Sh LANGUAGE
$0 is the record, $1 through $NF are its fields. FS and RS select field and record separators. OFS and ORS control print. NR and FNR count records. FILENAME, ARGC, ARGV and ENVIRON expose invocation state. Additional variables include SUBSEP, CONVFMT, OFMT, IGNORECASE, FIELDWIDTHS, FPAT and selected PROCINFO keys.
.Pp
Programs may use associative and nested arrays, functions, recursion, if, for, while, do, break, continue and return. Built-in operations include print, printf, sprintf, split, patsplit, sub, gsub, gensub, match, index, substr, length, tolower, toupper and mathematical functions. Call close() to release a redirected stream and collect a child.
.Sh SYSTEM ACCESS
The Darwin adapter operates with the calling account. The portable host interface denies file redirection, process creation and time access until the adapter supplies them. Native NovaOS delegation and revocation are described in the separate admission proposal.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
awk -F: '{print $1}' comptes.txt
cat journal.txt | awk '/erreur/ {print NR, $0}'
awk '{s += $1} END {print s}' nombres.txt
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Normal completion returns zero. An explicit exit supplies the program status. Syntax diagnostics return one and runtime, I/O and unsupported-option errors return two.
